# JavaScript Standards

- Use JavaScript (ES6+) only. Never add TypeScript, `tsconfig.json`, or `.ts` / `.tsx` files.
- Use ES modules (`import` / `export`). Better Auth does not support CommonJS.
- Prefer named exports. Use `const` / `let`. Never `var`.
- Use `async` / `await`. Handle errors explicitly; do not swallow them.
- Keep functions small. Put reusable pure helpers in `src/utils/`.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
async function loadOrder(id) {
  try {
    return await Order.findById(id);
  } catch (e) {}
}

// ✅ GOOD
export async function loadOrder(id) {
  const order = await Order.findById(id);
  if (!order) {
    throw new AppError("Order not found", 404);
  }
  return order;
}
```
